      {
        "path": "scene_runtime.frontier_gate.topic_pressure.topic:approach_around_away.last_answer",
        "value": "\"I'm not sure about the exact number,\" the tavern runner says with a shrug. \"They usually patrol in small groups, maybe half a dozen or so, but no one has said precisely how many went missing.\" They glance toward the gate serjeant, then lean in with a low voice, \"If you want to know more, you might check with the guard captain inside the gate—he keeps the rosters and might share what he's willing.\""
      },
      {
        "path": "scene_runtime.frontier_gate.topic_pressure.topic:find_information_perhap.last_answer",
        "value": "The muddied trail twists northwest, bordered by scattered broken banners whose frayed edges flutter in the damp wind. Their sigils match those worn on the missing patrol’s uniforms. Amid the ruins of the last known route, you spot subtle signs of hurried passage—broken twigs, faint footprints pressed deep into the soft earth. The air carries a faint hint of smoke, distant and elusive but unmistakably recent."
      }
